WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.290
So movement and motility is almost synonymous with life.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.720
When you peer inside the inner life of a cell with a microscope,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.810
you can see that it's churning with moving objects.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.560
Many of these moving objects are small cargo containers called 

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.480
membrane organelles or vesicles.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.710
These are essentially the delivery trucks of the cell.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.880
At the time we were doing this experiment in 1984, we really didn't have 

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.250
answers to those fundamental questions of how that motility occurs,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.150
so our goal was to figure it out.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:45.250
So we figured if we were going to understand motility,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.730
we should look at it in a system which has 

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.670
the highest concentration of all of these motility components, these moving organelles,

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.080
the motor proteins,

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:02.250
and that's why we picked the axon. The axon is effectively 

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.970
a dedicated highway to molecular transport.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.160
A nerve cell,

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.620
unlike a liver cell or many other cells,

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.350
is extraordinarily long.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.080
One part of the cell may be in your spinal cord,

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.820
but the other end of that same cell,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.720
may be at the tip of your toe. And in between that cell body in your 

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.250
spinal cord and your toe is a very,

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:33.140
very long tube that's called the axon, that connects these 

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.450
very distal parts of the same cell.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.610
And this is essentially like shipping things between one part of the 

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:45.330
country and the other. Of all the axons that you can possibly choose,

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.660
which one would you choose?

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.080
Well,

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.360
we decided to work on the squid giant axon.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.650
It is a much larger axon than an axon that you would 

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.380
find in a mammal,

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.050
for example,

00:01:59.050 --> 00:01:59.750
or a human.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.930
We made the guess that this would be a good 

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:09.570
hunting ground to try to find which are the 

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:14.100
motor machineries that are causing this form of 

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.330
axonal transport.

